# mtk-tpd: the touchscreen, as an input device for keys.
#
# With double tap to wake on, the Ilitek driver reports the double tap as the
# power key (scancode 116). As WAKEUP instead, the double tap goes through
# LineageOS's check of the proximity sensor before turning the screen on
# (Settings > Display > Prevent accidental wake-up), which the framework only
# applies to WAKEUP: a double tap in a pocket stays dark. The power key itself
# is on mtk-kpd and is not affected.
#
# Nothing else on this device sends keys: the keys the input device declares
# besides it are never reported by the driver.
key 116   WAKEUP
